33,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, it's a bit scary! Most of our costs are fixed things like hall hire and insurance, and a lot of people struggled to pay their renewals on time.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"That is concerning. I found that turnout for weekday meetings dropped significantly after the summer outings, and some quieter members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's even worse than I thought. A tiny group of us are doing all the work and attending everything, while some people pay the same fee and never even show up.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The administrative side is equally taxing. Chasing individual payments takes hours every month, and calculating partial fees for mid-year joiners is a tedious, manual process.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found out that a lot of people who came to taster evenings didn't join because a full year's fee was too much at once, and old named grades caused friction!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, if chasing individual payments is that hard, maybe we should avoid any system that requires collecting money at every single event.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Mio. If we make the cost of attending a weekday meeting a conscious decision each time, we might see that turnout drop even further.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"I'm still stuck on the fairness part. If we just do one flat fee, the people who are here every week and doing all the setup are basically subsidizing the people who never show up.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"While I understand your point, Takumi, a complex system to ensure ""fairness"" often increases the administrative burden I just described. We must balance equity with practicality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"Maybe we could find a middle ground? I don't want to scare off new people with a huge upfront cost, but I also don't want the treasurer to be miserable!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, that's the tricky part! If we lower the upfront cost, we might end up with more of those manual calculations and chasing that @Toshio mentioned. We need a way to keep it simple but accessible.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I wonder if we can find a way to keep the atmosphere welcoming. If people feel they are paying for something they aren't using, they might stop coming altogether.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"But if we make it too cheap or optional, the people who actually run the place will just get more resentful. We can't ignore that a few of us are doing everything.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we implement a system based on usage, we risk increasing the workload for the treasurer to an unsustainable level. We must consider the cost of the labor required to manage the fees.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"What if we had different levels? That way, people who come a lot can pay more, and new people don't have to pay for a whole year right away!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"That sounds like a possibility, Kenji! But we have to be careful that it doesn't make the bookkeeping a nightmare for whoever takes over the treasurer role.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am also concerned that tiered levels might create a social divide, making some members feel like second-class citizens if they cannot afford the higher tier.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm more worried about the people who are already doing the work. If we have tiers, will the people who do the setup and locking up be in a different group than the ones who just show up?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Regardless of the social grouping, the primary issue is the volume of transactions. Any system that requires constant monitoring of who is in which tier will be a burden.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I just want us to find something that feels fair to everyone and doesn't stop people from joining! Let's see what the actual options are before we worry too much.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
