59,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Okay, here are the options! We have A: a Flat Annual Fee, B: Tiered Membership, and C: Activity-Based Charging. Looking at our findings, A seems the simplest for the treasurer.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I disagree with Option A. Given that turnout dropped when we introduced charges and some members feel uneasy about the cost per visit, a large upfront fee might further discourage attendance.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A is just as unfair as before. Why should the people who are here every week pay the same as someone who shows up twice a year? Option B seems better.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B could work, but only if the tiers are set at the start of the year. Option C is completely out of the question; the administrative burden would be unbearable.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I'm leaning towards Option B too! It lets new people join without a huge cost and avoids the friction of the old named grades if we do it right.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Jonathan, if we go with B, we can keep the entry tier low so it's not a barrier. But @Takumi, wouldn't a flat fee actually be fairer for the regulars since it's the cheapest per visit?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Perhaps, but the psychological barrier of a large sum upfront is the issue. Option B allows people to commit at a level they feel comfortable with, preserving the welcoming atmosphere.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, it's only ""cheaper per visit"" if they actually come. Right now, the regulars are paying for the hall and insurance while others get a free ride. Option B lets us acknowledge different levels of commitment.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"If we choose Option B, we must ensure the tiers are fixed annually. If members can switch tiers mid-year, we are back to the manual calculations and administrative chaos I warned about.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with Toshio! As long as we keep the tiers simple and set them once a year, it should be easy to manage and welcoming for everyone.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Jonathan, if we keep the tiers simple, it shouldn't feel like a barrier. I'm starting to think Option B is the best compromise between the treasurer's sanity and the members' needs.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I can agree to Option B, provided the tiers are designed to be inclusive and do not create a sense of hierarchy that might alienate our quieter members.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm satisfied with Option B. It addresses the imbalance of usage and effort while still being a structured system that doesn't require chasing people every single week.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is acceptable, provided the rules for each tier are clear and the payment is collected upfront. It is the only viable alternative to Option A that doesn't destroy the treasurer's free time.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm all for Option B! It seems like the only way to make everyone happy—the regulars, the newcomers, and the treasurer. Let's do it!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I think we've reached a consensus then! Option B balances the costs, the workload, and the welcoming feel we want. I'll cast my vote for Option B.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Option B is the most balanced choice for our community. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,It's the only way to make it fair for those of us putting in the work. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"Since it avoids the chaos of activity-based charging while offering more flexibility than a flat fee, I vote for Option B.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm so glad we all agree! I vote for Option B too!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
